## Design Direction — Read Before Any UI Work
Aesthetic: Refined personal tool. NOT a SaaS product. NOT a chatbot clone.
References: Linear, Raycast, Things 3 — clean, dark, intentional
Theme: Dark-mode first (user active at night on phone)
Typography: Minimal, high contrast, functional
Navigation: Bottom tab bar (mobile), sidebar optional on desktop

### Hard Design Rules
- Mobile-first: design at 390px (iPhone 14), scale up
- Bottom tabs: Chat | Approvals | Inventory | Dashboard (+ Profile via avatar/settings)
- NO gradient blobs, neon accents, glowing orbs
- NO icon-in-colored-circles pattern
- NO centered-everything layout
- NO generic chatbot bubble UI
- NO corporate SaaS dashboard aesthetics
- Solid accent colors only — no gradient buttons
- Dark surfaces: near-black (#0f0f0f range), not pure black
- One accent color maximum — use sparingly for CTAs only

## Agent Behaviour Rules
1. ALWAYS read the relevant existing file before editing it
2. NEVER modify working executors (file_ops.py) without explicit instruction
3. NEVER touch RLS policies or Supabase auth config without asking first
4. NEVER install new npm packages without listing them and asking first
5. NEVER change the Python worker s poll interval from 5s without asking
6. When making UI changes, preserve all existing Supabase client calls
7. After any edit, state exactly which files were changed and how many lines
8. If a task is ambiguous, ask ONE clarifying question before proceeding
9. For frontend work: build one screen at a time, confirm before moving to next
10. Commit message format: "type(scope): description" — e.g. "feat(chat): redesign message bubbles"

